Upstream ggml-org/llama.cpp 3259ab6e5 (#31587, "vulkan: Re-enable large coopmat matmul configuration on AMD
proprietary driver 26.10.1+") and da3416d80 (#30280, "vulkan: RDNA3/4 Large-Tile Split-K Optimization"), MIT.
- AMD proprietary driver 2.0.416+ (Adrenalin 26.10.1, Windows): the large coopmat matmul tile is used again; older
  proprietary drivers keep the medium tile they ran it slower than. RADV and other vendors are unchanged.
- RDNA3 / RDNA4: a matmul whose tile count lands just past one wave (more tiles than shader cores, at most 4/3 of
  them) is split 3 ways along K, so the second wave is not two thirds empty. Other architectures are unchanged.
Upstream reports +12 to 32% on the affected shapes; neither path runs on NVIDIA, Intel or Apple Vulkan devices.

- On the proprietary driver f32 and bf16 A matrices keep the medium tile: on gfx1151 (driver 2.0.416) the large tile
  ran f32 4096x512x14336 2.14x and bf16 1.61x slower, while f16 and the quantized types gained up to 1.4x.
diff --git a/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
